<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia to host meeting on energy with U.S.</title>
<headline>Colombia to host meeting on energy with U.S.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-03-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. and Colombian government officials and private sector entrepreneurs will meet on Colombia's Caribbean coast for a three day-bilateral energy summit starting April 7, a statement from the Mines and Energy Ministry said on Sunday.</p>
<p>Representatives of Colombia's Mines and Energy Ministry and the U.S. Department of Energy will head the list of delegates at the Colombia-USA Bilateral Energy meeting in the port city of Cartagena.</p>
<p>Agenda items include technical and environmental cooperation, information exchange and investment opportunities in the gas, coal, oil and electricity generation sectors, One of the cornerstones of Colombia's President Ernesto Samper's economic program is wider private sector participation in the energy sector.</p>
<p>((-- Karl Penhaul, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
